## Deployments ##
> A deployments in kubernetes is used to manage and run your application pods.
Deployment
    ↓
ReplicaSet
    ↓
Pods
    ↓
Container
    ↓
Application

> for example :- if you want 3 nginx Pods, you don't normally create 3 Pods manually. 
> You create a Deployment:
nginx-deployment
       ↓
   ReplicaSet
       ↓
 ┌─────┼─────┐
Pod-1 Pod-2 Pod-3

> The Deployment continuously makes sure the desired number of Pods are running.


> <<<<<<>>>>>> {why we use deployment} <<<<<<>>>>>>

> without deployment:

You create Pod
     ↓
Pod crashes
     ↓
You manually create another Pod 

> with deployment 

Deployment
     ↓
Pod crashes
     ↓
Kubernetes automatically creates replacement Pod 

>**** deployment also provide ****

Scaling — increase/decrease Pods
Rolling updates — update application without stopping everything
Rollback — go back to previous version
Self-healing — maintain desired Pod count
Version/revision history

